  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening Migration and Border Management Capacities in Bosnia and Herzegovina</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Since 2017, there has been a significant increase in the number of migrants and asylum seekers transiting through Bosnia and Herzegovina (BiH). While the efforts made to enhance the capacities of migration authorities in BiH have led to improvements in the management of the migration response, important challenges persist due to the dynamic nature of migration flows, logistical difficulties to ensure coverage of vast and remote border areas, high staff turnover, complicated coordination and cooperation mechanisms across borders and within the country, evolutions in the legislative and operational contexts, as well as limited budgetary resources. This project will support BiH authorities to effectively manage mixed migration flows and strengthen border management capacities, in alignment with the relevant EU and international standards. More specifically, the project will support building of technical and operational capacities of border management authorities in BiH, notably through joint training on cross-border patrols, as well as technical equipment and software. Through coordinated field exercises, data collection and analysis, the project will also provide access to dynamic migration information and knowledge exchange platforms to inform policy and operational decisions. Lastly, interventions will support skills building and inclusion, by leveraging innovative partnerships and engaging in communities.</narrative>
  </description>
